---
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import RevealText from '../components/RevealText.astro';
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { link, repository } from '../lib/site';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Project principles — ZeroCloud"
  description="ZeroCloud’s principles: control of your data, connections between your devices, and security by default."
>
  <div class="frame">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ text: 'Home', href: link() }, { text: 'Project' }]} />
    <header class="page-lead">
      <p class="eyeline" data-enter>The project</p>
      <h1 data-enter><RevealText text="What ZeroCloud means." /></h1>
      <p data-enter>
        Zero required cloud services. Your devices can work together while you keep control of your
        data and the connections you choose.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2 data-enter><RevealText text="When the internet goes out" /></h2>
      <p data-enter>
        Two devices on the same reachable network can keep communicating even when that network
        loses internet access. ZeroCloud is built around that distinction. Essential workflows
        should continue on hardware the user controls.
      </p>
      <h2 data-enter><RevealText text="Your devices hold the data" /></h2>
      <p data-enter>
        The design calls for processing and storage on the device. When you choose to share
        something, the intended destination is the device you selected. Finding a peer should also
        be possible locally.
      </p>
      <h2 data-enter><RevealText text="Secure by default" /></h2>
      <p data-enter>
        Encryption is a requirement for the data an app stores or exchanges. Access should be
        explicit and controlled by you. These requirements guide every app we are building.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href={repository}>Read the project repository ↗</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
